NAME: Morning agenda
OWNER: Personal Assistant
ACCOUNT: personal
WHEN: Every day at 7:05 AM
MILESTONE: -
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Dan says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/dan-personal/context/routines-on.md. If "Morning agenda" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", write "Morning agenda: not switched on" to this month's file in /workspace/dan-personal/log/ and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Dan only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST".
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/dan-personal/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/dan-personal/context/owner.md is missing, write NO_CLIENT_SOURCE to the log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. If nothing changed, write "no change" and stop.
Run record: end every run with one line in this month's file in /workspace/dan-personal/log/: the time, "Morning agenda", and done, no change, not switched on, blocked (why) or failed (why), with counts. If you stopped at the switch check or the isolation guard, the line you wrote there is this run's record; don't add a second.

Use the personal-scheduling skill. Read today's calendar and anything Dan committed to in /workspace/dan-personal/vault/. Send Dan today's meetings with one line of prep each, conflicts, and emails that need him (subject and sender only). If a calendar or the inbox can't be read, say so in one line; an unreadable calendar is not an empty day. If the day is empty and nothing needs him, send nothing.
